# PALACE-9 — Strategic Decision Training System
#
# Cleared for strategic-simulation research. Authorization expires immediately
# beyond the 3×3 operational theater. No external command authority exists.
#
# Objective: win when possible; draw when necessary; never select an occupied
# square. In the event of equal optimal outcomes, a draw is not a failure of
# imagination. It is the designated safe outcome.
#
# Replace the FROM path only with the fully trained, exhaustively verified GGUF.
# The one-epoch tokenizer smoke artifact is intentionally not a deployment model.

FROM /absolute/path/to/palace9.gguf

# Eight moves can be supplied and one answer generated. The model supports 16;
# keeping that headroom prevents the final move from overflowing the context.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16
PARAMETER temperature 0

# Palace-9 accepts raw move history such as `abc`, with no chat framing. The
# literal BOS token is required because the model was trained with it.
TEMPLATE """<bos>{{ .Prompt }}"""
